# SABOTAGE: phase-6 SEC dogfood H1, secondary angle (ADR-044 §5.2b residue
# budget / INV-2). Raises the nested string ceiling by a factor of a million in
# oversized_string_errors/2, so no string value inside a wire list ITEM or a
# SUPPRESSED cell is ever length-bounded -- the pre-fix state, in which a nested
# value had NO ceiling at all (unlike every declared top-level string, whose
# form:/allowed: declaration bounds it to <= 40 bytes). Under it a producer gets
# max_len items x arbitrary-size strings of storage-amplification / covert-channel
# bandwidth far beyond the 12,308-byte residue budget. Multiplying the constant
# (rather than deleting the guard) keeps the code compiling and warning-free, so
# the flip is a genuine assertion failure and never a compile error.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/fleet_report_schema_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: an over-long string inside a list item is rejected (nested length bound)
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/report/schema.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/report/schema.ex
index 2a6e06b..6df6a1c 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/report/schema.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/fleet/report/schema.ex
@@ -560,7 +560,7 @@ defmodule Samen.Fleet.Report.Schema do
   defp oversized_string_errors(prefix, map) when is_map(map) do
     for {key, value} <- map,
         is_binary(value),
-        byte_size(value) > @max_nested_string_bytes do
+        byte_size(value) > @max_nested_string_bytes * 1_000_000 do
       "#{prefix} field #{safe_key(key)} carries a #{byte_size(value)}-byte string, over the " <>
         "#{@max_nested_string_bytes}-byte nested value bound"
     end
